---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

/**
 * The one page in this project that is not the instrument. It is static markup
 * with no island: the argument does not need a clock, and shipping React here
 * would mean the manifesto costs more to load than the app it describes.
 *
 * `/manifesto/`, not `/manifest/`: `/manifest.webmanifest` already exists and
 * means something else entirely.
 *
 * This does not break the one-route rule. That rule is about `/api/*` on the
 * Worker; a second static page is another file in `dist/`, served by the assets
 * binding, costing the product nothing.
 *
 * It states, it does not explain. Nothing here describes a feature, names a
 * file or defends a decision: that is what `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` are for,
 * and a manifesto that reads like release notes is neither.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Manifesto · circal"
  description="Your calendar draws time as a line. A line promises that today ends somewhere further on. It does not."
  scroll
>
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[36rem] px-6 pt-14 pb-24 sm:pt-20">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-ink-2 transition-colors hover:text-ink"
      aria-label="Open circal"
    >
      {/* The mark itself: black disc, one thin white circumference. */}
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-[15px]" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"
        ></circle>
      </svg>
      <span class="text-[15px] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em]">circal</span>
    </a>

    <h1
      class="mt-14 text-[34px] leading-[1.08] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em] text-balance text-ink sm:text-[44px]"
    >
      A day is a circle.
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-7 text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-2">
      Your calendar draws time as a line. A list running down, a week running right, hours stacked
      like receipts. A line makes a promise: that today ends somewhere further on.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[21px] leading-[1.4] font-medium tracking-[-0.015em] text-ink">
      It does not. You go the whole way around and arrive back at the hour you left.
    </p>

    {
      /* Two up on a phone: at four across, a tile is 78px and the week's seven
        faces are 11px each, which is a smear rather than an argument. */
    }
    <figure class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-4 sm:gap-3">
      <div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="26" fill="none" class="stroke-ink-4" stroke-width="1.25"
          ></circle>
          <path
            d="M51.92 15.29A26 26 0 0 1 48.71 51.92"
            fill="none"
            class="stroke-accent"
            stroke-width="3"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <path
            d="M21.01 55.56A26 26 0 0 1 9.48 45"
            fill="none"
            class="stroke-ink-3"
            stroke-width="3"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <path
            d="M39.97 32.7 57.9 34.27"
            class="stroke-ink"
            stroke-width="1.25"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Day</figcaption>
      </div>

      <div>
        {
          /* Seven faces at one rotation: the arcs sit at the same angle on
            every circle, which is the whole of what the week view says. The
            faces can only ever be a seventh of the tile wide, which is the
            strip's own constraint, so the strokes are the thinnest thing on
            the page: at 1.4 the arc was 40% of the radius and each face read
            as a filled blob rather than a face with something on it. */
        }
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          {
            [4.57, 13.71, 22.86, 32.0, 41.14, 50.29, 59.43].map((cx) => (
              <g>
                <circle cx={cx} cy="32" r="4" fill="none" class="stroke-ink-4" stroke-width="0.6" />
                <path
                  d={`M${(cx + 3.06).toFixed(2)} 29.43A4 4 0 0 1 ${(cx + 3.98).toFixed(2)} 32.35`}
                  fill="none"
                  class="stroke-accent"
                  stroke-width="1.1"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                />
              </g>
            ))
          }
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Week</figcaption>
      </div>

      <div>
        {
          /* A dashed circle is a ring of marks for the price of one element;
             365 <line>s would be 20 KB of decoration. */
        }
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle
            cx="32"
            cy="32"
            r="25"
            fill="none"
            class="stroke-ink-3"
            stroke-width="6"
            stroke-dasharray="0.9 1.35"></circle>
          {
            /* A day carrying something is a *longer* mark, not a fatter one:
              `markRadius` grows outwards, so this matches the ring's own
              dash width and outreaches it. */
          }
          <path d="M48.47 18.18 55.75 12.07" class="stroke-accent" stroke-width="1.3"></path>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Year</figcaption>
      </div>

      <div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <defs>
            <pattern id="m-lived" width="5.2" height="5.2" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <circle cx="1.3" cy="1.3" r="1.05" class="fill-ink-2"></circle>
            </pattern>
            <pattern id="m-left" width="5.2" height="5.2" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <circle cx="1.3" cy="1.3" r="1.05" class="fill-ink-4"></circle>
            </pattern>
          </defs>
          <rect x="5" y="8" width="54" height="22" fill="url(#m-lived)"></rect>
          <rect x="5" y="30" width="54" height="26" fill="url(#m-left)"></rect>
          <circle cx="27.1" cy="24.9" r="1.35" class="fill-accent"></circle>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Life</figcaption>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <p class="mt-7 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
      A day, a week, a year, a life. One shape at four distances. Every one of them turns, and every
      one of them comes back around.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="label text-ink-3">The return</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        Every day issues you the same twenty four positions. The same nine in the morning. The same
        dead hour after lunch. Nothing new is minted. The face you are handed today is the face you
        were handed yesterday, wiped.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        <strong class="font-medium text-ink"
          >That is the oldest fact about being alive, and it is the one a calendar is usually built
          to help you forget.</strong
        >
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="label text-ink-3">A line can always be longer</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        Which is the whole appeal of it. Add a row. Add another. A list will absorb anything you put
        on it and it will never once tell you the day is full.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        A circle cannot lie like that. It is one revolution wide and that is all it will ever be.
        Put two hours on it and two hours are gone, in ink, and the room they took is room nothing
        else can have.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        <strong class="font-medium text-ink">This is not a productivity feature.</strong> It is a mirror,
        and most days it is not flattering.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="label text-ink-3">You get about twenty nine thousand</h2>

      <blockquote class="mt-4 border-l border-hairline pl-4">
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.5] text-ink-3 italic">You are a worm through time.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <p class="mt-5 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        One dot for every day of a life. They fit on a single screen, which is the alarming part and
        also the useful one.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        Some of them are already spent. Nothing on that grid says whether they were spent well, and
        nothing ever will. It does not grade you. It counts.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Look at it once.</strong> Then go and put something on tomorrow.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="label text-ink-3">Nobody else is holding these</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        Your days live in this browser. No account, no server, no copy of your life on somebody
        else's machine. Nothing measured, nothing sold, nothing trained on you.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        {
          /* Explicit space: Astro drops the newline between a text node and an
            element that starts the next line, so `transfer.If` renders. */
        }
        That is a promise, and it is also a transfer.{" "}
        <strong class="font-medium text-ink"
          >If nobody else is keeping your calendar, then you are.</strong
        > Export it. Keep a copy. And stop waiting for a company to take your time seriously on your behalf,
        because not one of them ever has.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="label text-ink-3">Go round again</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        The return is not the punishment. It is the offer.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        Tomorrow the light on the rim goes back to nothing, the face comes up empty, and you get the
        same twenty four hours as everybody who has ever done anything at all.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-2">
        Fill it on purpose or leave it empty on purpose. Both are decisions.{" "}
        <strong class="font-medium text-ink"
          >Drifting is the only thing on that face that is not.</strong
        >
      </p>

      <p
        class="mt-10 text-[24px] leading-[1.3] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance text-ink"
      >
        The circle closes so that it can open.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-hairline pt-8">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-[9px] bg-ink px-4 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-void transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
      >
        Open circal
      </a>
      <p class="caption mt-6 text-ink-3">
        “You are a worm through time” is the opening line of the Hiss incantation, from Control
        (Remedy Entertainment, 2019).
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
